> Actual source performance

These measurements come from the complete source run above; each series retains source execution order. A bounded run or one evaluation point does not establish convergence. Model loss and task return use separate figures.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/alphazero_diagnostic0.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto data=dm::nn::load_npz("build/alphazero_source.npz");auto it=std::find_if(data.begin(),data.end(),[](const auto&v){return v.first=="wins";});auto all=it->second.to_vector<double>();auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();for(int opponent=0;opponent<2;++opponent){std::vector<double>x,y;for(size_t j=opponent;j<all.size();j+=2){x.push_back(j/2==0?1:(j/2)*5);y.push_back(all[j]);}plot.lines(x,y,opponent?"versus MCTS(200),20 games":"versus random,40 games",{37+opponent*150,99,235-opponent*150});}plot.title("AlphaZero original wins by opponent").x_label("Self-play iteration").y_label("Game count").size(1100,600).save_svg("build/alphazero_diagnostic0.svg");}
